-- Why a separate table rather than columns on material_aliases: an equivalence decision has its own
-- lifecycle (PENDING for months, REJECTED on evidence, superseded by a better reference) and each
-- step must survive. The alias stores only the RESULT — its basis and the decision that authorised
-- it. The hand-written half of this change (VERIFIED requires an APPROVED decision) lives in the
-- companion migration 20261031140100_d2_constraints_and_immutability, because Prisma cannot express
-- CHECK constraints. Both are applied in one `prisma migrate deploy`.

